</th> <th>Test</th> </tr> <tr> <td>Templated</td> <td>13,928</td> <td>400</td> <td>1,000</td> <td>66,535</td> <td>1,827</td> <td>1,000</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Automatic</td> <td>153,441</td> <td>1,750</td> <td>2,750</td> <td>737,114</td> <td>8,025</td> <td>2,750</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Multi Answer</td> <td>23,929</td> <td>400</td> <td>1,000</td> <td>112,736</td> <td>1,844</td> <td>1,000</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Two Hop</td> <td>21,040</td> <td>400</td> <td>1,000</td> <td>99,866</td> <td>1,895</td> <td>1,000</td> </tr> <tr> <th data-level=\"0\"><strong>Total</strong></th> <td><strong>212,338</strong></td> <td><strong>2,950</strong></td> <td><strong>5,750</strong></td> <td><strong>1,016,251</strong></td> <td><strong>13,591</strong></td> <td><strong>5,750</strong></td> </tr> <caption><strong>Table 3: Question type counts by train / val / test split.</strong></caption> </table>","bad":null,"sourceImages":[{"src":"/documents/conventions/a1d5725d79ff-zoo-figure-cards-p6.png","sha256":"a1d5725d79ffacae18bac500accdb564c6d58621e30980858f5b431850953f11","bytes":236529}]},{"id":"6","name":"Sample — a two-sided balance sheet in one frame","kind":"sample","constructed":false,"paragraphs":["Assets down the left, liabilities and equity down the middle, an income statement on the right, all inside one ruled box under two title bands. These are different schemas, not consecutive ranges of a repeated schema. Repeated-schema continuations follow Column Continuation§9.3.2 even inside one enclosing frame. Row n on the left has nothing to do with row n in the middle, and yet this is one table, row n across all blocks — the frame is one grid and is transcribed as the grid it prints. The side-by-side rule above is for boxes with their own frames."],"tables":[{"label":"Expected Markdown","rows":[[{"text":"Balance Sheet","header":true,"colSpan":4,"rowSpan":1},{"text":"Income Statement","header":true,"colSpan":2,"rowSpan":1}],[{"text":"Millions of yen","header":true,"colSpan":4,"rowSpan":1,"runs":[{"text